  <p>
    <strong>White label vs private label activewear</strong> is one of the first sourcing decisions a new fitness brand, yoga studio or retailer needs to make. Both routes can put your name on activewear, but they do not offer the same level of control over the product, the development work or the collection’s long-term differentiation.
  </p>
  <p>
    The terminology is not perfectly standardized across apparel suppliers. The useful question is therefore not only “Which label do you offer?” It is “Who controls the style, fabric, fit, color, branding and future use of the product?” This guide turns that question into a practical buyer brief for leggings, sports bras, yoga sets and gym wear.
  </p>

